# Responsive UI — mobile-first (VCP / Topcoat)

Every interactive Topcoat screen (`view!` pages / components) must
render without horizontal overflow on a 375 px-wide phone and adapt
cleanly up to desktop. Patterns adapted from the bastion responsive
lessons (issue-driven), without Askama / HTMX assumptions.

## Tables

- Wrap `<table>` in a horizontal scroll container (`overflow-x-auto`).
- Hide non-essential columns at small breakpoints
  (`hidden sm:table-cell`, `hidden md:table-cell`, …).
- For each column hidden on mobile, surface its data inside the
  primary visible column (`sm:hidden` / `md:hidden` block) so nothing
  is silently lost.
- Prefer `break-words` / `break-all` (emails, hostnames, IDs, license
  keys display forms) over forced `whitespace-nowrap` on long tokens.

## List rows

- Row containers: stack on phone, row on larger breakpoints
  (`flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between`).
- Metadata lines: `flex flex-wrap … gap-x-2 gap-y-1`.
- Bullet separators that crowd phones: hide at base
  (`hidden sm:inline`).

## Headers and toolbars

- Titles scale by breakpoint (`text-xl … sm:text-2xl lg:text-3xl`);
  avoid a single large fixed title size on `<h1>` / `<h2>`.
- Action bars wrap (`flex flex-wrap gap-2`); do not force a single
  non-wrapping row of buttons on phones.
- Fixed-width helpers (IDs, status chips): `truncate min-w-0` or
  `hidden sm:inline`.

## Floating containers

- Toasts / dropdowns must not pin a fixed `w-96` at the base
  breakpoint; prefer `w-full max-w-md` (optionally `sm:w-96`).

## Padding and breadcrumbs

- Dense card padding: `px-4 sm:px-6` rather than bare `px-6` at base.
- Breadcrumbs: allow horizontal scroll (`overflow-x-auto` +
  `whitespace-nowrap` on the list) instead of pushing the layout.

## Layout

- Prefer stacked (`flex-col`) layouts that become rows from `sm` / `md`.
- Avoid fixed widths like `w-96` at the base breakpoint; use
  `w-full max-w-*` instead.
- Test critical paths at 375 / 768 / 1280 before hand-off.

## Why

Hard-coded desktop widths and unscoped `whitespace-nowrap` are the
usual sources of horizontal scroll on phones. When a structural lint
exists for `view!` / Tailwind classes, run it locally before hand-off.
